    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d196">

                <pb facs="0284" n="272" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg272"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.60D/100a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Finland</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">McClintock</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-24T20:00:00-04:00">April 24, 1943—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>74. You will delay action contemplated in my 72, April 23, 2 p.m. until further
                    instructions. Please acknowledge receipt of this message immediately stating
                    whether it was received in time.<anchor n="67" xml:id="d196-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d196-f1" n="67" xml:id="d196-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 595, April 25, 10 a.m., the Chargé acknowledged receipt of the
                    telegram and said that he would cancel the appointment with the Finnish Foreign
                    Minister scheduled for that same day (124.60D/101).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
